Package: gog
Title: Grammar of Graphics
Version: 0.6.2
Authors@R:
    person("psychometrician", role = c("aut", "cre"), email = "psychometrician@gmail.com")
Description: Draw a plot by describing it. You name a table, a mark to
    draw, and which column goes to which part of the picture. This
    specification uses the same words in R, 'Python', 'Julia' and
    'JavaScript', and one engine, written in 'Rust', draws it as an SVG
    in all four. On macOS and Windows the engine comes with the
    package. On Linux the install compiles it, which needs 'Rust' 1.75
    or newer.
License: Apache License (== 2.0)
URL: https://github.com/psychometrician/gog,
    https://psychometrician.github.io/gog-book/
BugReports: https://github.com/psychometrician/gog/issues
SystemRequirements: Cargo (Rust's package manager), rustc (>= 1.75)
Encoding: UTF-8
Depends:
    R (>= 4.3)
Roxygen: list(markdown = TRUE)
Imports:
    jsonlite,
    utils
Suggests:
    DBI,
    RSQLite,
    gapminder,
    IRdisplay,
    knitr,
    pkgload,
    repr,
    testthat (>= 3.0.0)
Config/testthat/edition: 3
